{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And I will give the rain of your land.</b> You do what is upon you, and I too will do what is upon Me (ibid.)." "<b>In its time.</b> At night, so as not to trouble you. Another interpretation: בְּעִתּוֹ — on the nights of Sabbaths, when everyone is at home." "<b>The former rain.</b> It is the rainfall that falls after the sowing, which saturates the earth and the seeds." "<b>The latter rain.</b> The rainfall that descends close to the harvest, to fill the grain in its stalks. And the meaning of מַלְקוֹשׁ is something delayed, as we translate (Genesis 30): ״וְהָיָה הָעֲטֻפִים לְלָבָן״ — לַקִּישַׁיָּא [the late ones]. Another interpretation: it is called מַלְקוֹשׁ because it descends upon the ears of grain and upon the stalks." "<b>And you shall gather your grain.</b> You shall gather it into the house — and not your enemies, as in the matter stated: ״אִם אֶתֵּן דְּגָנֵךְ וגו׳ כִּי מְאַסְפָיו יֹאכְלֻהוּ״ (Isaiah 62) — and not as in the matter stated: ״וְהָיָה אִם זָרַע יִשְׂרָאֵל וגו׳״ (Judges 6)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:34.549382284Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}